<article class="env-lemma" id="04GU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04GU">Lemma <span data-tag="04GU">10.155.10</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a local map of local rings. Choose separable algebraic closures $R/\mathfrak m_ R \subset \kappa _1^{sep}$ and $S/\mathfrak m_ S \subset \kappa _2^{sep}$. Let $R \to R^{sh}$ and $S \to S^{sh}$ be the corresponding strict henselizations. Given any commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \kappa _1^{sep} \ar[r]_{\phi } &  \kappa _2^{sep} \\  R/\mathfrak m_ R \ar[r]^{\varphi } \ar[u] &  S/\mathfrak m_ S \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
  <p> There exists a unique local ring map $R^{sh} \to S^{sh}$ fitting into the commutative diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ R^{sh} \ar[r]_ f &  S^{sh} \\  R \ar[u] \ar[r] &  S \ar[u] }  \]
</div>
  <p> and inducing $\phi $ on the residue fields of $R^{sh}$ and $S^{sh}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/08HR" data-tag="08HR">10.154.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>